desc: Sharp Practice Stereo Detuner (mda Detune port) by chmaha
tags: pitch detune doubler stereo widener
author: chmaha
version: 1.0
changelog:
  Initial release.
about:
  A simple stereo detuner for thickening and widening. The left and right inputs are summed and pitch-shifted by a few
  cents, down for the left output and up for the right, then mixed with the dry signal on each side. Detune sets the
  offset (0 to 300 cents, finest at the bottom of its range), Mix balances dry and detuned, Output sets the level, and
  Latency sets the length of the crossfaded chunks (about 6 to 93 ms at 44.1 kHz): longer chunks suit sustained sounds,
  shorter ones keep percussive sounds tighter. The display shows the two crossfading read heads of each shifter.
  The buttons at the top load the original's three programs: Stereo Detune, Symphonic (the same settings as
  Stereo Detune in mda's code) and Out Of Tune.
  Ported from mda Detune by Paul Kellett (Maxim Digital Audio), via mda-effects
  https://github.com/pluginguru/mda-effects (MIT or GPLv2+)
  JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license
  Claude generated some of this code
